  "id": "COMPOUND:15568 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate to the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 through a series of molecular interactions. Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate is directly implicated in the target of two distinct entities, one of which is the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, and the other is 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. Both of these entities are known to be targets of specific compounds, which in turn interact with the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This indicates a possible pathway where Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate may influence the activity of these enzymes, which in turn modulate the function of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. The evidence is supported by a consistent chain of targets, suggesting a plausible mechanistic link. However, the exact nature of the interaction between Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 remains unclear, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate in this process.",
